WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.920
I may be out of line asking logical questions about a Doctor Seuss story,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.240
but I gotta ask one that's been bothering me since I was very, very young.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.360
What the heck is a Grinch?

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.800
Biologically, I mean.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.120
He's a furry green monster that lives alone in a snowy cave,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.260
there seems to be only one of him,

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.390
he hates everyone and yet he still owns a dog...

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:32.600
According to the poem, he can slither like a snake through the who houses

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.040
and according to the lyrics of "You're a Mean One, Mr Grinch",

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.880
at various times, he's a "crooked jerky jockey",

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.480
a "nasty-wasty skunk"

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.880
and a "greasy black banana".

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.000
I mean, Internet!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.640
Your guess is as good as mine

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.740
Or I guess, my guess is as good as mine.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.340
'Cause I know at some point, I'm gonna have to be the one to answer my own question, aren't I?

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.240
*sigh*

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.160
It's lonely being a theorist sometimes!

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:08.720
*Intro theme*

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.700
Hello Internet! Welcome to Film Theory!

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.207
The show that'll warm the cockles of your heart

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:18.300
and then inspire you to look up what cockles actually are.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.119
Fun fact!

00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:21.569
Apparently they're small bivalve molluscs,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.732
and the reason we say "cockles of our hearts"

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.900
is because somebody hundreds of years ago mixed up the Latin word for "Snails"

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.560
with the Latin word for "ventricle" and we just never bothered to fix it.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.560
"Oh yeah!"

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.139
Anyway, with ethically compromised holiday of Thanksgiving behind us,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.880
it's time that we go straight into Christmas mode!

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.460
'tis the season for nostalgic remembrances of advent calendars,

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.620
elementary school pageants, (all the cringe)

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.920
and walking through the aisles of Toys "R" Us (rest in peace)

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.080
all while being enchanted by things like dolls with stretchy arms,

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:56.780
and uncomfortable pieces of plastic that will bruise the bejesus out of your ankles!

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.120
But it's important to consider that not everybody remembers those times so fondly,poop

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.140
of course, I'm talking about the Grinch.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.020
One of the most plainly evil characters in all of the western canon.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.909
Sure, I can get behind some anti-heroes who make questionable ethical choices,

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:18.749
but stealing the source of joy from all the Who children in all of Whoville is simply beyond the pale.

00:02:18.749 --> 00:02:23.780
Of course, The Grinch also has one of the most memorable turnarounds of any villain that I can think of,

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:29.160
when he brings everything back to the Whos and more importantly has a very literal change of heart.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:35.220
To use the original source material, we should say that the Grinch's heart "grew three sizes that day"

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.755
Now, I'm not sure what old Doc Seuss meant by "three sizes",

00:02:38.755 --> 00:02:41.700
hearts don't come quite as standardized as khakis.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.280
But by the looks of that visual representation,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.329
the only Christmas miracle here is if the Grinch's heart doesn't crack a rib!

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:53.900
But the question I have today is how much of this is a tall Christmas tale,

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.106
and how much of it could actually happen?

00:02:56.106 --> 00:03:00.100
Could the Grinch survive his heart growing three sizes,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.120
or is the end of "How the Grinch Stole Christmas" an awful lot like the middle of "Alien"?

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.940
Was it really the Christmas spirit that made his heart swell, or is there something else to blame?

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.945
Is the end of one of our all-time favorite Christmas stories

00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:17.820
a tragic disaster instead of a heartwarming tearjerker?

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:24.140
All coming up on this episode of Grinch's Anatomy where we're gonna need 50 cc's of theorizing stat!

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:29.180
If we're gonna consider the ramifications of the Grinch's heart suddenly going where no heart has gone before,

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.260
we have to first consider the state his heart is in.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:39.240
We're told right off the bat, that the narrator believes that the reason the Grinch hates Christmas is that his heart is two sizes too small.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.480
"two sizes too small."

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.720
It might seem like that should be enough to kill the Grinch outright,

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.100
But tiny hearts are indeed a thing among human beings,

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.519
and since the Grinch talks, and stands upright, and owns a dog,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.800
We are for the sake of simplicity gonna compare him to a human being

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.680
when it comes to whatever crazy heart condition he has.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.800
Small heart syndrome is a relatively uncommon (and uncreatively named) condition

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.080
that results in low Oxygen levels in the blood,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:07.320
and a tendency towards extreme fatigue, even after normal levels of physical activity.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.211
Research also shows that having a small heart makes it vastly more likely

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.680
that the individual will have Chronic Fatigue Syndrome,

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:17.386
I know I'm starting to sound a bit like one of those minute long commercials

00:04:17.386 --> 00:04:18.810
that come on during "The Price Is Right",

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.080
but trust me that I'm going somewhere with all this.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:25.380
Chronic Fatigue Syndrome or CFS makes you feel constantly tired,

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:30.008
puts you in a sort of mental fog, gives you sleep problems, poor circulation,

00:04:30.008 --> 00:04:33.600
and makes you more sensitive to external stimuli, like noise.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.340
We can see from his general Grinchy shape

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:40.920
that the Grinch is definitely skipping leg day, and arm day, and ab day.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.625
So we definitely have evidence pointing to fatigue and lethargy,

00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:45.400
and all that stuff about poor circulation,

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:50.039
which would cause cold hands and feet may explain why the Grinch bothers to wear shoes...

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.720
...but neglect pants.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:57.440
The real clincher here though is that not only does Chronic Fatigue Syndrome factor into the Grinch's small heart,

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.080
it also perfectly explains why he hates Christmas in the first place.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.919
His rationale is mentioned casually at the beginning of the movie...

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:06.919
"There's one thing I hate..."

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.140
"All the noise, noise, noise, noise!

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:14.680
If the Grinch has trouble sleeping in the first place due to his Chronic Fatigue Syndrome,

00:05:14.969 --> 00:05:18.256
which also then makes him particularly sensitive to noise,

00:05:18.256 --> 00:05:21.769
I gotta say that I kind of feel some sympathy for the poor guy.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.879
Not only is he a societal outcast who lives by himself in a snowy cave,

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.340
but he's got himself a chronic condition,

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.721
and the only people he ever gets to see

00:05:30.721 --> 00:05:32.680
love to make a big hootenanny,

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.380
and make his life even more miserable with their cheerful sounds.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:42.180
And it's not like he's trying to kill all the Whos, or burn down Whoville, or steal their stuff on a regular basis,

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:47.360
One time on the one day of the year, he just wanted to not be made miserable,

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.720
and have his health problems exasperated.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:52.680
And all of a sudden he's this terrible person for life.

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:58.699
Call me Grinch Pat, but I think that the Grinch's actions are actually kinda defensible.

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:01.098
I mean trust me, as the father of an infant son,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:05.320
I have a new found understanding of the desperation for a good quiet night asleep.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.540
Whatever that is, I can't even remember anymore.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:11.940
and let's not forget that the Grinch doesn't even succeed at stealing Christmas,

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.901
he feels guilty and gives it all back.

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:16.759
Why do we hate this guy?

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:20.628
I mean, they don't make super villains out of people who are guilty of attempted murder,

00:06:20.628 --> 00:06:25.560
so why is this guy the worst, when his only crime was attempted holiday theft?

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:30.100
Could it be that the Grinch is actually the hero of Christmas?

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.740
No, clearly not, and even if he was that would be for a very different episode.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.439
"STAY FOCUSED!"

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:37.609
So the TLDR is that the Grinch has Chronic Fatigue Syndrome,

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.810
and a teensy ticker with the elevated heart rate and blood pressure that goes with it.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:47.479
So what does it mean for his prognosis when his heart suddenly plumps up like me after three rounds of Thanksgiving turkey?

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:49.758
Well, it depends on what's going on,

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:53.363
but the most likely explanation is that the Grinch has had a heart attack,

00:06:53.363 --> 00:06:55.068
and a subsequent myocardial rupture.

00:06:55.069 --> 00:06:59.483
I know! Old cartoons are very scary, especially from a medical perspective.

00:06:59.483 --> 00:07:01.249
So what does all of that mean?

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:05.840
Well when this happens, it means that one of the valves in his heart bursts open,

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:12.040
letting all the blood that's very carefully regulated in and out of your heart rush in until the pressure equalizes,

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:16.020
and that might sound like an extreme leap for a green Christmas monster,

00:07:16.039 --> 00:07:20.449
but tons of details in the story line up with this sort of diagnosis.

00:07:20.449 --> 00:07:24.060
Let's start with the fact that again, due to his Chronic Fatigue Syndrome,

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.720
the Grinch is indeed pretty out of shape.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.360
Even if that big Grinch wagon is doing just fine!

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:34.100
And yet all Christmas night, he's been running around from house to house, climbing up and down chimneys,

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:39.160
javelining Christmas trees around, all while carrying the presents of the entire town with him.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.480
His muscles are going to be exhausted,

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.450
and that includes the muscles in his heart.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:50.260
but then we get the clincher - the sequence when the Grinch's sled almost runs over the top of Mount Crumpit,

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.060
and he sees the error of his ways.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:57.100
He finds the Who resilience charming, and so he sprints up the rest of the mountain,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.560
a mountain we are expressly told is ten thousand feet high,

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:04.180
"Ten thousand feet up."

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.500
"Up the side of Mount Crumpit."

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:12.120
"He rode with his load, to the tip-top to dump it."

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:15.234
Grabs the sled, loaded with about eight tons of presents,

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.820
and then his heart grows three sizes,

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.400
to the point that it looks like it should explode out of his ribcage!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.519
While this may all look like he's just moved by the spirit of Christmas,

00:08:25.519 --> 00:08:28.780
in reality he's just moved by a lot of neurotransmitters.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:34.000
Hmm, nothing to take that magical feeling out of the holiday season like explaining it away with biology

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.050
I know how to have myself a good holiday!

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:39.440
You see when the Grinch notices the sled starting to go over the top,

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.420
he's gonna have himself a moment of panic,

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.140
you know, that sinking jumping feeling in your stomach,

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:47.720
when you realize a big problem, or you have yourself a bad surprise.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.420
That feeling is adrenaline and noradrenaline coursing through your body.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.180
High levels of those hormones are the ones that are gonna give you that dizzy excited feeling,

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.360
while also allowing you to run faster,

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:00.767
or suddenly gain super strength in a moment of extreme need.

00:09:00.767 --> 00:09:04.560
Those are the stories that you hear about parents lifting cars off their children,

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.049
people racing long distances to escape danger,

00:09:07.049 --> 00:09:11.780
or in our case, rescuing a town-full of Christmas presents from the edge of a cliff.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.440
In this moment, he has, to quote the movie:

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.280
"Found the strength of ten Grinches, plus two!"

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:25.094
Unfortunately, the other thing that a large sudden spike of those hormones can create is a massive heart attack.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.071
In particular, the sudden stress may cause arterial plaque to dislodge

00:09:29.071 --> 00:09:31.340
and clog up the heart with a blood clot.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:34.440
This itself isn't gonna cause the Grinch's heart to explode,

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:38.760
but it does give us a pretty good explanation for what we see in the cartoon.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.260
Myocardial ruptures which cause the heart to swell up,

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.780
almost always occur in the aftermath of a heart attack.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:49.060
A Cardiologist from Johns Hopkins, named Dr David Cass,

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:53.500
actually discussed what could have caused the Grinch's heart to grow three sizes quickly,

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:57.100
and one of his possible diagnoses was a ruptured valve.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.920
Though he ultimately rules it out by saying that the Grinch wouldn't have felt so good when it was happening.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:04.319
"You're not gonna be handing out lots of presents, and, you know, being cheerful,"

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:07.120
"so, that part didn't really fit so much."

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.400
But, let's consider how the Jim Carrey version of The Grinch reacts when his heart is growing three sizes.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.300
Roll the tape!

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:18.720
*Grinch screaming*

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:22.120
"I'm...feeling!"

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.740
I don't know about you, but it looks like he's having some sort of coronary episode to me,

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:31.880
but even if you're bothered by the fact that the Grinch in the animated version isn't having any kind of visible trauma,

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:35.100
that doesn't mean that he hasn't had a heart attack.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:40.600
Some studies indicate that as many as 45% of people who have had heart attacks

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:43.740
don't realize that they've actually had one.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:49.060
Even the Grinch's sudden warming towards the Whos may be evidence of this heart attack.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:54.600
The lack of blood to the brain during the heart attack sometimes causes feelings of euphoria for the sufferer.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:58.060
So while there is no Grinch doctor on the scene to confirm in the moment,

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:03.919
the fact is that there's a high likelihood that the Grinch's heart wasn't receiving jolts of holiday joy and cheer,

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:10.360
it was receiving jolts of adrenaline that overloaded his systems and literally caused his heart to short-circuit!

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.340
*lightning*

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:12.425
So then what happens?

00:11:12.425 --> 00:11:15.320
Well, now the Grinch's heart is blowing up like a balloon,

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:20.270
But he'll probably be fine, right? Christmas...spirit and all that?

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:24.900
Well, it depends on how severe the situation is, but it ain't looking too great.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:29.200
Up to 82%of people who experienced some form of cardiac rupture,

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.380
Will die within two weeks if it isn't noticed and treated immediately.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:36.600
If the rupture is severe enough that it breaks through the wall of the left ventricle,

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:41.220
(and judging by the visuals,that heart is breaking through every wall that's remotely near it)

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:45.880
The mortality rate jumps up to 100.0%

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:50.569
Thanks, by the way, researchers, for including that ".0" in there for emphasis.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:57.940
Anyway you shake it, The Grinch is almost certainly dead within hours or days of the movies ending.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:01.640
Even if you refer back to the book, you see him carving the roast beast at the end,

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:07.099
But he's just as dead as the Beast on his plate, because there is no chance that he sees another holiday season.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:09.340
So what have we learned here today, friends?

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:14.277
Quite simply, that Christmas cheer is a deadly thing, and MatPat is the biggest Scrooge of them all!

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.640
But you don't have to take my word for it,

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.374
The answer has been hidden since the very beginning.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.660
Just look at the lyrics to "You're A Mean One, Mr Grinch"

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:27.441
"Your heart's a dead tomato, splotched with mouldy purple spots."

00:12:27.441 --> 00:12:30.000
Dead tomato, with purple spots...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.860
Hmmmm...

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:34.960
Oh yeah, it was there the entire time.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.860
You're a mean one, Mr Seuss!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:43.720
But hey, that's just a theory, a Film Theory!

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:44.700
aaand...

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:48.180
did you notice the subtle nod to my new headphones in this theory?

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:51.400
I wasn't just jamming out to some radical holiday tunes while I wrote this episode,

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.200
Mannheim Steamroller Christmas, take me away!

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.220
These are actually my new go-to headphones from Dolby.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.120
Not that particular about all my technology,

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:04.100
but as a guy who spends all day listening to YouTube videos, and does a show that's entirely voiceover,

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.200
and has to watch a lot of movies for his job,

00:13:06.209 --> 00:13:09.181
audio is *the* thing that makes a huge difference for me.

00:13:09.181 --> 00:13:11.980
For this episode, Dolby offered to sponsor us

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:17.520
and asked if I wanted to try out their new never-before-tried Dolby Dimension headphones

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.100
CHRISTMAS PRESENT ALERT!

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:23.320
They literally hand-delivered these things to me, because they weren't released to the public yet.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:28.980
I wasn't even allowed to let other people in the office see these things, but let me tell you, they are incredible.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:32.360
now that they've officially been announced, and I can actually show them to people in the public,

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.180
I wear them every day.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.080
I take them on road trips, plane rides,

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.240
basically I just live in these things now.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:41.004
And the difference between me being so excited about these headphones,

00:13:41.004 --> 00:13:43.140
and less so about headphones I've worn in the past,

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.260
is a feature that you would never expect.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:50.020
It's actually one that allows you to choose how much ambient noise you hear in the headset.

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.860
It's called "Dolby Lifemix".

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:54.020
If I'm working with other people on a theory,

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.960
or, I need to be able to hear a video and also hear someone talking at the same time,

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:01.780
I can just adjust the headphones that I can hear both completely clearly

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:07.160
It's insane, the headphones take voices from the outside and amplify them based on my preferences

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.760
directly into my ear, so I can hear exactly what's being said.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:14.640
While I'm still immersed in what I'm watching or listening to.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.660
Then, if I want total noise cancellation,

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.630
like on a plane, where if Jason's talking to me,

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.700
(because lord knows I don't want to hear Jason talk)

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.410
I can just double tap the ear, and poof! All that noise is gone!

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.481
No more one headphone on, one headphone off,

00:14:26.481 --> 00:14:29.540
which has literally been how I've listened to headphones for years,

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.069
and it kind of goes without saying but the sound in these things is incredible.

